# Kafka Plugin — runnable .http examples
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. Control Plane API running locally (default: http://localhost:5149)
#   2. Kafka__BootstrapServers / Kafka__MonitoredConsumerGroups / Kafka__DlqTopics
#      set in .env.local (never commit real broker hosts — see SECURITY.md)
#
# Secrets: never commit real broker addresses or credentials here.
# HOST/PROJECT_ID come from .env by default via {{$dotenv ...}}; override them in
# your local .env.local (gitignored) instead of editing this file.

@HOST = {{$dotenv HOST}}
@PROJECT_ID = {{$dotenv PROJECT_ID}}

###
# Replay a Kafka dead-letter topic to the primary processing topic.
# RequiresConfirmation=true — the UI asks for confirmation before executing.
# This is currently a stub: see ReplayKafkaDlqOperation.ExecuteAsync.

POST {{HOST}}/api/operations/execute
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{PROJECT_ID}}",
  "operationId": "replay-kafka-dlq",
  "requestedBy": "engineer@example.com",
  "input": {
    "topic": "example-topic.dlq"
  }
}

###
# Retrieve the last 20 operation executions (includes Kafka plugin history).

GET {{HOST}}/api/operations/history?take=20
Accept: application/json
